WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:03.280
Welcome to the city of the future.

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:06.080
A smart city that knows everything
about you.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:09.280
From how you like your coffee,
to whether you've broken the law.

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:11.360
Or even if you've grown a beard.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:12.520
Sound far-fetched?

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:16.600
While the smart city we're about
to tour doesn't exist yet,

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.160
all of the parts do.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.080
They're all components
of real projects

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.760
happening all over the world.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.720
Put them together and this
is what life may well be like

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:26.400
in the not-too-distant future.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:30.440
You go to work, your office building
knows exactly who's coming and going

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:33.360
and what they need, thanks to
thousands of inbuilt sensors

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:34.480
collecting data.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.880
The energy efficient building
is designed for your comfort,

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:40.320
reacting to changes in the weather
and the number of people

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:43.440
in the building and adjusting
its climate accordingly.

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.960
Wherever you sit, the lighting will
adjust to suit your preferences.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.520
The building will even recall
your regular coffee order

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:51.960
and there's no chance of it
getting your name wrong.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:57.480
On your way home, you pass lamp posts
laden with sensors and HD cameras

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:01.040
that monitor and record
the world around them 24/7.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:03.720
Air quality and traffic flow data
tell you the quickest

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:07.480
and cleanest route and alert
emergency services to accidents.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.560
You arrive home, to a nutritious meal
made from locally grown avocados

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:15.400
using hydroponics,
so no need for soil.

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:19.480
Sensors allow urban farmers to make
constant adjustments to temperature,

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:22.320
light and water and monitor
the plant's responses,

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:26.040
so it's easier and cheaper
to grow fresh food in cities.

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:29.320
The level of control smart
technology gives can also be used

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:30.720
to make food tastier.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:35.360
In Singapore, they've already found a
way to make kale sweeter and softer,

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:38.440
so even the fussiest of eaters
will enjoy their greens.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:43.000
Your health is flourishing, thanks
to your perfectly balanced diet

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:46.840
but you also regularly update your
doctors using data sent directly

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:48.080
from your smartwatch.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:52.040
They analyse it and prescribe
personalised drugs and supplements

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:54.680
that are quickly 3D printed
just for you.

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:59.720
Your baby stirs and you're alerted
by its smart blanket.

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:02.960
Reassured that all is well,
child mortality rates are at an

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:07.680
all time low, you go to bed but the
sensors in the street never sleep.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:11.880
They're busy policing antisocial
behaviour, identifying people smoking

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:16.080
in unauthorised zones or throwing
rubbish from high-rise buildings -

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:17.760
crime rates are negligible.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:22.200
While much of this might sound pretty
idyllic, it is not without issues.

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:26.080
Smart cities go hand-in-hand with
gathering and storing huge amounts

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:29.080
of personal data
and using it to control city life.

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:31.760
For governments keen to control
certain populations,

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:34.120
this is an incredibly powerful tool.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:38.440
Every moment of your daily routine
can be tracked, anyone with access

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:42.240
to this data can find out where you
live, where you go every day,

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:45.040
the places you visit at night
and who you're with.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:48.560
This data can be used by people
with far more nefarious aims

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:50.640
than making you
the perfect soya latte.

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:54.600
You could leave your phone at home,
with an advanced facial recognition

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:58.400
CCTV in the mix, authorities can
easily keep tabs on you.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:02.400
In places like Xinjiang in China,
where growing a beard can already

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:05.440
get you reported,
this is a frightening prospect.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:09.200
So are the benefits of a smart city
worth giving up privacy

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:10.240
and freedom for?

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:14.320
Can governments and corporations
be trusted with such huge data sets

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:17.160
on all of us? What happens
if there's a mistake in the system

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:20.200
or you want to overthrow
the system itself?

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:23.680
Whether you think smart technology
means we're sleepwalking

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:27.960
into a dystopian future or enabling
us to live a vastly more convenient

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:32.320
and sustainable lifestyle, it's
coming soon to a city near you.

